    "title": "Wolves Take Down Mavs On Road - Minnesota News Network",
    "text": "(Dallas, TX) — For the second straight game the Timberwolves put forth a dominant performance as they beat the Mavericks 118-105 on Wednesday night in Dallas. Julius Randle had 31 points for the Timberwolves, who have now won two straight after dropping five in a row. Naz Reid had 23 points off the bench and Anthony Edwards also contributed 20 points in the victory. The Wolves improved to 29-19 and the win moved them into sixth place in the Western Conference and, at least for the time being, out of the play in tournament. Minnesota is back in action tonight when they host Oklahoma City for an 8:30 P-M tip from Target Center.\nAfter the game, Alan Horton checked in with Naz Reid on the Timberwolves Radio Network:",
